     "rationale": "Mixed: (c) retention/switching-cost -- genuine, via a 20-year PPA with Meta (2,609 MW nuclear capacity/energy, PJM plants) signed Jan 2026, real long-dated customer lock-in. Nuclear capacity itself has real scarcity value (long lead times and regulatory barriers make it hard to replicate) -- a legitimate, if narrow, structural advantage. But (a) pricing power and (b) margin-vs-industry not evidenced -- most of the ~40GW+ fleet still sells into competitive wholesale markets, and the stock trades as part of a correlated \"AI power\" basket (with NRG/CEG/TLN) driven by sentiment on AI capex payback, not a demonstrated pricing moat. Only 1 of 4 cross-checks clearly evidenced -- held at 3, not pushed to 4-5.",
